<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gallienus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 218–268</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a> · Also known as Publius Licinius Egnatius Gallienus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gallienus was Roman emperor from 253 to 268, first with his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valerian">Valerian</a> and alone after Valerian's capture by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persians">Persians</a> in 260. His reign saw the worst of the 3rd-century crisis: the Gallic and Palmyrene regions broke away, and Alemanni, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goths">Goths</a> and others invaded. He defeated the Alemanni near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a>, reorganised the cavalry, and was murdered by his officers in 268.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gallienus.jpg" alt="Gallienus" width="320" height="394" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sailko · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ritratto_di_gallieno_dalla_casa_delle_vestali.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
